WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Here's what people
are talking about.

00:00:01.368 --> 00:00:02.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
The big story today
was that Congress

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:05.839
had just one day left to prevent
a government shutdown.

00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:08.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
But don't worry --
it'll only affect nonessential

00:00:08.108 --> 00:00:10.243 size:78% position:39%
government employees,
like park rangers,

00:00:10.243 --> 00:00:12.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
museum guides,
and the President,

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:16.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
so that'll be fine.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:17.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
I guess Congress
had 24 hours to pass

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:21.187
a short-term spending bill if
they want to avoid a shutdown.

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:22.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
Trump told them
to do their jobs,

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:24.324 align:start size:94% position:6%
then went back
to announcing the winners

00:00:24.324 --> 00:00:25.792 line:92%
of a made-up awards show.

00:00:25.792 --> 00:00:27.927 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:28.561 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Did you see this?

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:33.133
Last night, Trump tweeted a link
to his Fake News Awards page,

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:35.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
but for a while,
it wouldn't load.

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:37.103 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:37.771 size:81% position:41% line:92%
His I.T. guy was like,

00:00:37.771 --> 00:00:40.974
[ Russian accent ] "Sorry, my
trolls can only build so fast."

00:00:40.974 --> 00:00:41.975 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:41.975 --> 00:00:45.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I'll get back
to working on this thing."

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:47.347 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Heh heh heh."

00:00:47.347 --> 00:00:48.515 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.515 --> 00:00:50.717
[ Normal voice ] But Trump
named "The New York Times,"

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:56.456
ABC News, and CNN as the top
three reporters of fake news.

00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:59.959
And his top three reporters
of real news were Fox News,

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:02.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
his Magic 8-Ball,
and Snapple caps.

00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:05.131 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:08.568 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Real news.

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:09.235 size:75% position:38% line:92%
This is interesting.

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:11.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
I read that Trump
actually has two cellphones,

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:14.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
and his staff nicknamed them
Trump 1 and Trump 2.

00:01:14.841 --> 00:01:16.810
Sounds a little something
out of a Dr. Seuss book.

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:18.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
It's actually no coincidence.

00:01:18.445 --> 00:01:21.681
Trump actually wrote his own
Dr. Seuss book about himself.

00:01:21.681 --> 00:01:25.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
We got a copy.
Check this out. It says...

00:01:29.089 --> 00:01:31.558 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:36.930 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:42.368 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:47.740 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.716 --> 00:01:58.118 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:58.118 --> 00:02:00.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's not
a great book for kids.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:03.056 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:06.559 size:81% position:41% line:92%
♪♪ Cov-fefe, cov... ♪♪

00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:07.660 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:09.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
Ooh, check this out.
Dunkin' Donuts.

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:10.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
I love Dunkin' Donuts.
-Oh, the Dunk.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:13.299
-Dunkin' Donuts is opening some
new stores around the country

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:16.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
that are just called Dunkin'.
-Yeah.

00:02:16.236 --> 00:02:16.803 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:19.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They're saying
they're next-generation stores

00:02:19.539 --> 00:02:20.373 size:81% position:41% line:92%
for younger customers.

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:22.675 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I think they might
be trying a little too hard

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:23.977 line:92%
to appeal to millennials.

00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:25.345 line:92%
Check out their latest ad.

00:02:25.345 --> 00:02:27.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
-'Sup teens?
Can you even?

00:02:27.881 --> 00:02:29.782 line:92%
We can, 'cause we're Dunkin'.

00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:32.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're not your parents'
coffee place.

00:02:32.452 --> 00:02:32.886 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Lame!

00:02:32.886 --> 00:02:35.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
Our new stores
are totally tilted.

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:36.756 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪ Tilted ♪♪

00:02:36.756 --> 00:02:39.159 align:start size:94% position:6%
That other coffee?
-Corporate.

00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:40.560 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Know what I meme?

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:44.297 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-I can has coffee, meow?

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:45.865 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-R-R-R-R-Reboot!

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:46.766 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Explosion ]

00:02:46.766 --> 00:02:47.767 size:75% position:38% line:92%
[ Air horn blaring ]

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:48.868 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
D-a-a-amn, Dunkin'!

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:51.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're so cool,
we're coming to Hulu.

00:02:51.771 --> 00:02:52.438 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Stream!

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:54.841 line:92%
-So fidget spin on into Dunkin'.

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:56.276 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
We're the G.O.A.T.!

00:02:56.276 --> 00:02:57.844 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Goat screams ]

00:02:57.844 --> 00:02:59.279 line:92%
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:02:59.279 --> 00:03:00.513 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-What?

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:03.650 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:08.488 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.488 --> 00:03:09.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow!
-Yeah.

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:10.456 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, I know.

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:12.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like -- I think they're
trying a little too hard.

00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:13.326 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You think
they're trying too hard?

00:03:13.326 --> 00:03:15.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A little bit, man.
-[ Laughing ]

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:19.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, my goodness.
[ Laughing ]

00:03:19.265 --> 00:03:20.934 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Get this, you guys.

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:23.803 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.803 --> 00:03:24.437 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's tilted, man.

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:26.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Fidget spin
your way over here."

00:03:26.339 --> 00:03:27.707 size:75% position:38%
-Yeah, fidget, yeah.
[ Air horn blaring ]

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:30.143 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I know.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:30.143 --> 00:03:32.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
I saw that --
I saw that two new

00:03:32.245 --> 00:03:35.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
axe-throwing bars
will open in Boston this year.

00:03:35.715 --> 00:03:36.849 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:38.618 size:81% position:41%
That's right -- Boston
is getting a new bar

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:40.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
where people
can try axe-throwing.

00:03:40.687 --> 00:03:44.157
So far, all the customers
give it 1 1/2 thumbs up.

00:03:44.157 --> 00:03:48.394 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:50.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
And finally,
a little sports news.

00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:52.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
Sunday is the
AFC Championship game

00:03:52.565 --> 00:03:55.001 align:start size:94% position:6%
between the Patriots
and the Jaguars.

00:03:55.001 --> 00:03:58.004 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:58.004 --> 00:04:01.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I saw that Tom Brady
injured his hand.

00:04:01.841 --> 00:04:02.675 line:92%
People said, "What happened?"

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:04.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
He said, "You know
that new axe-throwing bar?"

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:08.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
We have a great show tonight.
Give it up for The Roots!

